From: kevin03L <kevin03L@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc/tegra: pmc: let the GPU driver clamp the GPU rail

The GPU's clamp can be removed (tegra_pmc_powergate_remove_clamping()) but not set again. NVIDIA's
L4T clamps the GPU before it turns the GPU rail off; without it the memory controller sees the
unpowered GPU's outputs, and memory errors or a hung board can follow the next power-up.
nvgpu-nano uses this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c	2026-11-24 17:14:00.931082657 +0100
+++ b/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c	2026-11-24 17:14:00.987081471 +0100
@@ -1109,6 +1109,27 @@
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(tegra_pmc_powergate_remove_clamping);
 
 /**
+ * tegra_pmc_powergate_gpu_clamp() - clamp the GPU partition
+ * @pmc: power management controller
+ *
+ * The GPU has its own power rail: isolate it before the rail is turned off.
+ * tegra_pmc_powergate_remove_clamping() removes the clamp again.
+ */
+int tegra_pmc_powergate_gpu_clamp(struct tegra_pmc *pmc)
+{
+	if (!pmc->soc->has_gpu_clamps)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	mutex_lock(&pmc->powergates_lock);
+	tegra_pmc_writel(pmc, 1, GPU_RG_CNTRL);
+	tegra_pmc_readl(pmc, GPU_RG_CNTRL);
+	mutex_unlock(&pmc->powergates_lock);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(tegra_pmc_powergate_gpu_clamp);
+
+/**
  * tegra_pmc_powergate_sequence_power_up() - power up partition
  * @pmc: power management controller
  * @id: partition ID
--- a/include/soc/tegra/pmc.h	2026-11-24 17:14:00.935082571 +0100
+++ b/include/soc/tegra/pmc.h	2026-11-24 17:14:00.987081471 +0100
@@ -151,6 +151,7 @@
 int tegra_pmc_powergate_power_on(struct tegra_pmc *pmc, unsigned int id);
 int tegra_pmc_powergate_power_off(struct tegra_pmc *pmc, unsigned int id);
 int tegra_pmc_powergate_remove_clamping(struct tegra_pmc *pmc, unsigned int id);
+int tegra_pmc_powergate_gpu_clamp(struct tegra_pmc *pmc);
 
 /* Must be called with clk disabled, and returns with clk enabled */
 int tegra_pmc_powergate_sequence_power_up(struct tegra_pmc *pmc,
@@ -182,6 +183,12 @@
 {
 	return -ENOSYS;
 }
+
+static inline int
+tegra_pmc_powergate_gpu_clamp(struct tegra_pmc *pmc)
+{
+	return -ENOSYS;
+}
 
 /* Must be called with clk disabled, and returns with clk enabled */
 static inline int
